<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Essad Pasha Toptani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1863–1920</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Essad Pasha Toptani was an Ottoman general and Albanian landowner who surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkoder">Shkodër</a> to Montenegro in 1913 and then set up a rival government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durrës</a>, the Republic of Central Albania. He served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-prince-of-albania">Prince Wilhelm of Wied</a> before being exiled for intrigue in 1914, returned to rule central Albania until 1916 with Serbian and Italian backing, and was assassinated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/essad-pasha-toptani.jpg" alt="Essad Pasha Toptani" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Auguste Léon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1913_Essad_Toptani.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
